    "title": "MORE propaganda from the \"alleged famine\" in Gaza",
    "text": "Daily videos for months. Staged in ruins, makeup applied. This child is not malnourished. #GazaStarving pic.twitter.com/sqquP72tKd\n— Leslie Young ✡︎ (@AkaLazarus) July 30, 2025\nEven the kid cracked up mid-performance pic.twitter.com/mnTek9LMHd\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) July 30, 2025\nLike… seriously? That’s your spokesperson for famine? pic.twitter.com/I6lViYQW4T\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) July 26, 2025\nBoth videos were filmed in Gaza, at the same time. pic.twitter.com/DaKuXLPCxl\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) February 24, 2025\nWhile Hamas pushed a fake famine campaign, Gaza shops kept selling gold and perfumes — with cafes and event halls still open. The reality on the ground is far from what fooled the world\nAired this week on the main news edition of Israel’s Channel 14 @MaggieTabibi @Ahikam20 pic.twitter.com/Ozi6TyX5T4\n— C14 (@C14_news) July 30, 2025\nTens of thousands of tons were sent to Gaza to save them from a FAKE famine…\nWhile millions of people around the world are dying from REAL starvation.\nBut no one cares !!!😭\nBecause they can’t use it against Israel or the Jewish people.\nThe UN and its “humanitarian… pic.twitter.com/wSKSoFSH6Y\n— The Voice Of Truth 🙌 (@thevoicetruth1) April 22, 2025\nYou can’t run a “famine” campaign on an empty stomach, which is why Gaza’s restaurants keep thriving.\n(screen recording with sources starting at second 27) pic.twitter.com/UQoXc1gsjZ\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) July 29, 2025\nGAZA FAMINE HOAX\nGreat report by @SethAMandel about the fake famine in Gaza\nHere are the Main Points:\n1.Debunking the Famine Narrative:\n•A report by the Integrated Food Security Phase Classification’s Famine Review Committee reveals there is no famine in Gaza.\n•This… pic.twitter.com/v7zVOjDicg\n— Open Source Intel (@Osint613) June 23, 2024\nFilmed eating leaves. Directed to cry. Gaza’s children are props — and the UN still won’t comment. pic.twitter.com/3DcOzXOFmH\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) July 30, 2025\nDespite the hunger and lack of supplies, Gaza’s increasingly skeletal doctors keep pushing forward💪 pic.twitter.com/7adNpfbHUb\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) July 30, 2025\n🚨\nFABRICATED SUFFERING IS NOT EVIDENCE – IT’S PROPAGANDA!\nThis video of a newborn having a seizure, taken from a nursing page on FaceBook, is pushed by media outlets as a starving baby in Gaza.\nIf there are starving babies in Gaza, why do they fake the evidence? pic.twitter.com/0c3mV7zzHL\n— GAZAWOOD – the PALLYWOOD saga (@GAZAWOOD1) July 24, 2025\nFamine in Gaza?? @GAZAWOOD1 @truthmin1984 pic.twitter.com/Qnz1UW9gze\n— Traveling israel (@travelingisrae1) July 29, 2025\nThe New York Times has a lot to answer for. It’s hard to treat it as a publication that upholds journalistic values. The way the Times behaves is indistinguishable from tabloid journalism—hyping up “sensations” based on completely fabricated or distorted stories that fall apart… https://t.co/wNnpU4SdgF\n— Michael Livschitz (@MikeLivschitz) July 30, 2025\n﻿",
